  "thag10.5:6.1": "",
  "thag10.5:6.2": "The four-fold tie: greed, ill will, attachment to habits &amp; practice, and dogmatic obsession with views.",
  "thag10.5:6.3": "Floods: sensuality, becoming, views, and ignorance. See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn45.171'>SN 45:171</a>. These are identical with the four yokes. See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.10'>AN 4:10</a>.",
  "thag10.5:6.4": "Obsessions: sensual passion, resistance, views, uncertainty, conceit, passion for becoming, and ignorance. See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an7.11'>AN 7:11–12</a>.",
  "thag10.5:7.1": "Hindrances: sensual desire, ill will, sloth &amp; drowsiness, restlessness &amp; anxiety, and uncertainty. See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn2'>DN 2</a> and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51'>SN 46:51</a>.",
  "thag10.5:7.2": "",
